            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To ask for? (ਮੰਗਣਾ, maṅgṇā.) A request? (ਬੇਨਤੀ, bentī.) A little? (ਥੋੜ੍ਹਾ, thoṛhā.) A bit (to soften a request)? (ਜ਼ਰਾ, zarā.) To send for? (ਮੰਗਵਾਉਣਾ, maṅgvāuṇā.) Permission? (ਇਜਾਜ਼ਤ, ijāzat.) Forbidden? (ਮਨ੍ਹਾ, manhā.) Approved? (ਮਨਜ਼ੂਰ, manzūr.) An order? (ਹੁਕਮ, hukam.) To interrupt? (ਟੋਕਣਾ, ṭokṇā.) A refusal? (ਇਨਕਾਰ, inkār.) To back out? (ਟਲਣਾ, ṭalṇā.) An excuse? (ਬਹਾਨਾ, bahānā.) By no means? (ਹਰਗਿਜ਼, hargiz.) To dig one's heels in? (ਅੜਨਾ, aṛnā.) A promise? (ਵਾਅਦਾ, vāadā.) To persuade? (ਮਨਾਉਣਾ, manāuṇā.) Absolutely? (ਬਿਲਕੁਲ, bilkul.) To admit? (ਕਬੂਲਣਾ, kabūlṇā.) A compromise? (ਸਮਝੌਤਾ, samjhautā.) Doubt? (ਸ਼ੱਕ, shakk.) Certainty? (ਯਕੀਨ, yakīn.) Trust? (ਭਰੋਸਾ, bharosā.) A guess? (ਅੰਦਾਜ਼ਾ, andāzā.) To seem right? (ਜਚਣਾ, jachṇā.) To explain? (ਸਮਝਾਉਣਾ, samjhāuṇā.) Meaning? (ਮਤਲਬ, matlab.) A reason? (ਕਾਰਨ, kāran.) Plain to understand? (ਸਪਸ਼ਟ, sapshaṭ.) To suggest? (ਸੁਝਾਉਣਾ, sujhāuṇā.) To get muddled? (ਉਲਝਣਾ, ulajhṇā.) To slip up? (ਉੱਕਣਾ, ukkṇā.) A hint? (ਇਸ਼ਾਰਾ, ishārā.) A matter? (ਮਾਮਲਾ, māmlā.) Proof? (ਸਬੂਤ, sabūt.)"
